// EXPECT: no such function 'to_flot'
// A call to a name that is neither a function of this program nor a builtin.
// With no native backend attached there is nowhere it could be resolved from,
// so it is a typo -- and the message lists the builtins rather than leaving
// it to surface as an undeclared-function error from the C compiler.
main(int argc, string[] argv) {
  print(to_flot("1"));
} return int 0;
